{"annotationScore": 5.0, "comments": [{"commentType": "FUNCTION", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "15616305", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "17142766", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "17452329", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "18191790", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "20214904", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "20220136", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "24236072", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "27031443", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "35080426", "source": "PubMed"}], "value": "Effector molecule of the innate immune system that acts via antibiotic-like properties against a broad array of infectious agents including bacteria, fungi, and viruses or by promoting the activation and maturation of some APCs (PubMed:15616305, PubMed:17142766, PubMed:20220136, PubMed:24236072). Interacts with the essential precursor of cell wall synthesis lipid II to inhibit bacterial cell wall synthesis (PubMed:20214904). Inhibits adenovirus infection via inhibition of viral disassembly at the vertex region, thereby restricting the release of internal capsid protein pVI, which is required for endosomal membrane penetration during cell entry (PubMed:18191790). In addition, interaction with adenovirus capsid leads to the redirection of viral particles to TLR4 thereby promoting a NLRP3-mediated inflammasome response and interleukin 1-beta (IL-1beta) release (PubMed:35080426). Induces the production of pro-inflammatory cytokines including type I interferon (IFN) in plasmacytoid dendritic cells (pDCs) by triggering the degradation of NFKBIA and nuclear translocation of IRF1, both of which are required for activation of pDCs (PubMed:27031443)"}]}, {"commentType": "SUBUNIT", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "15064728", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "17452329", "source": "PubMed"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "24236072", "source": "PubMed"}], "value": "Tetramer (PubMed:24236072). Dimer (PubMed:17452329, PubMed:24236072). Interacts with RETN (PubMed:15064728)"}]}, {"commentType": "SUBUNIT", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "24236072", "source": "PubMed"}], "value": "(Microbial infection) Interacts with HIV-1 surface protein gp120"}]}, {"commentType": "SUBUNIT", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "17142766", "source": "PubMed"}], "value": "(Microbial infection) Interacts with herpes virus 1 (HHV1) envelope glycoprotein B; this interaction inhibits viral infection"}]}, {"commentType": "INTERACTION", "interactions": [{"interactantOne": {"intActId": "EBI-726336", "uniProtKBAccession": "P59665"}, "interactantTwo": {"geneName": "UBQLN2", "intActId": "EBI-947187", "uniProtKBAccession": "Q9UHD9"}, "numberOfExperiments": 3, "organismDiffer": false}, {"interactantOne": {"chainId": "PRO_0000006773", "intActId": "EBI-27090284"}, "interactantTwo": {"geneName": "S", "intActId": "EBI-25474821", "uniProtKBAccession": "P0DTC2"}, "numberOfExperiments": 3, "organismDiffer": true}]}, {"commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION", "subcellularLocations": [{"location": {"id": "SL-0243", "value": "Secreted"}}]}, {"commentType": "PTM", "texts": [{"value": "ADP-ribosylation drastically reduces cytotoxic and antibacterial activities, and enhances IL8 production"}]}, {"commentType": "PTM", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "id": "21904558", "source": "PubMed"}], "value": "Phosphorylation at Tyr-85 has been found in some cancer cell lines, and interferes with ADP-ribosylation"}]}, {"commentType": "SIMILARITY", "texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "value": "Belongs to the alpha-defensin family"}]}], "entryAudit": {"entryVersion": 198, "firstPublicDate": "2003-04-30", "last